It's far better than just an amulet of lifesaving. Need your whole
inventory ID'd really badly, and have a spare one of these scrolls
available? No problem...quit, write everything down, restore, ta-da, now
you know your whole inventory.

Run into a (M)MF and lose track of half the stuff in the game? Rollback!

Don't like how many charges your castle wand of wishing came with?
Rollback!

Plus, it pretty much frees up your neckslot since you don't need lifesaving
anymore.

About the only way I could possibly see this scroll being remotely balanced
for the game (and even then, it still wouldn't be) is that you need to be
alive to activate the rollback. So if you fall into a pit while carrying a
rubber chicken, then too bad, so sad. Maybe require a donation of 30,000+
gold, which the early game player won't have, and the late game player
won't want to carry.

It would need to come with some monumental drawbacks, for what it does.


